---
description: Run the project's own checks before and after a change
alwaysApply: true
---

# Verification

Find and run whatever gate this project actually has — a test script, a
`check_*.py`, a build. If it has one, a change is not done until it passes.

For anything visual, capture a screenshot and LOOK at it. Structural tests prove
structure and never prove appearance.

Commit only when the checks pass. Report which checks ran, what they returned,
and what remains unverified.
